<vertex eid="1"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Overview" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">H01 | E donor: gain and waveform</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">Current diagnosis; donor response, transfer, circuit and population subtrees can be active simultaneously.

Exact count; 1 ms timing and recovery delays; 1 mV voltage; 0.05 ms spike phases. No trace alignment or pooled override. Usable-tier separate.

Released/spent: I 0.23 nA; E sweeps 53 and 55. Still sealed in this snapshot: E sweep 54 (330 pA), I Noise1 sweep 48. No holdout opened by this artifact.

No simulations, fitting, morphology edits, or revival of stopped campaigns. Open/blocked leaves require separately registered and bounded experiments.

Legend: YES/NO = answered predicate, not physiological pass/fail. OPEN = valid question awaiting evidence; INCONCLUSIVE = attempted but no answer; BLOCKED = prerequisite or campaign boundary. Gray outcome boxes are conditional, not selected answers.

Overview links are navigation, not causal exclusions. Open the companion Markdown for the linked source index.

p014.md: Topographic diagnosis asks what is happening; do not begin with a root-cause label.
p018.md-p021.md: Binary questions cover all remaining possibilities and are quick, unambiguous and cheap; do not repeat the same split consecutively.
p035.md, p041.md: Retain the search as an explicit tree; classify the observation before selecting the decomposition.
p144.md: Functional Isolation: split the serial path and ask at which boundary the contrast remains.
p182.md-p183.md, p188.md, p192.md-p194.md: Structural Dissection: retain the complementary subsystem, interactions, and each written split.
p022.md, p074.md: Distinguish physical/mathematical constraints from man-made requirements. Use voltage/current and charge balance at electrical boundaries; no absolute-truth label for assumptions.</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.Boolean" key="noteVisible">false</attribute><attribute class="com.arciem.FuzzyBoolean" key="confidence"><fuzzyBoolean true="0.5"/></attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.operator.FuzzyOrVertexOperator" key="forwardOperator"><fuzzyOr/></attribute></attributes></vertex>
<vertex eid="2"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Overview" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">E donor: gain and waveform</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">Frozen B3 overfires at low drive; higher-drive count agreement does not settle phase width or return.

Navigation group; independent residuals can coexist.</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.Boolean" key="noteVisible">false</attribute><attribute class="com.arciem.FuzzyBoolean" key="confidence"><fuzzyBoolean true="0.5"/></attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.operator.FuzzyOrVertexOperator" key="forwardOperator"><fuzzyOr/></attribute></attributes></vertex>
<vertex eid="3"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered Yes" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">E01 [YES]
B3 has excess low-drive spikes?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">E01 | B3 has excess low-drive spikes?

Status: YES

Method: Hierarchical / input and cyclical

Scope / coordinates: B3 g0-b3; Allen 541563728; 200/250/310 pA; recorded bias; nseg x9; CVode 1e-10; 2100 ms.

Remaining search space: Low-drive exact-count agreement versus at least one excess-count row at 200/250 pA.

Binary predicate: At least one of the 200/250 pA model counts exceeds its matched human count.

Decision limit: Exact counts: human 1/5 at 200/250 pA; the 310 pA control is 10.

Recorded observation: B3 gives 4/8/10 versus human 1/5/10 at 200/250/310 pA.

YES: Localize the low-drive excess while retaining the 310 pA control.

NO: Low-drive excess is absent; inspect other response failures independently.

Next check: Use E02-E05 to retain tested exclusions; no additional evaluation is authorized.

Unresolved after either answer: Correct count at 310 pA is neither shared-input nor waveform validation.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-e-gain/stage-close-decision.json

