<vertex eid="9"><attributes><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="type">entity</attribute><attribute class="com.flyinglogic.logicgraph.entityclass.EntityClass" key="entityClass"><entityClass name="Answered No" uuid="fa010909-0000-4000-8000-000000000003"/></attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="title">E03 [NO]
Ih half meets the registered gain bands?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">E03 | Ih half meets the registered gain bands?

Status: NO

Method: Structural dissection / reversible intervention

Scope / coordinates: g1-ih-half versus B3, distributed Ih factor 75 to 37.5; SP3 stage G; same recorded inputs and controls.

Remaining search space: That tested intervention meets every registered gain/preservation band or fails at least one.

Binary predicate: g1-ih-half satisfies all stage-G gain and preservation clauses.

Decision limit: Use stage-g-decision arms/g1-ih-half/bands and rejection. The 250 pA count band is 5-7.

Recorded observation: 250 pA count remains 8; rest shifts -1.73 mV. The registered intervention is rejected.

YES: Retain this intervention as a candidate for independent validation.

NO: Exclude this Ih dose as a sufficient registered correction.

Next check: Carry the negative result to the next distinct tested split; do not repeat it.

Unresolved after either answer: Other Ih doses and interactions are not exhaustively excluded.

Evidence (repository-relative):
docs/evidence/h01-e-gain/stage-g-decision.json
docs/evidence/h01-e-gain/stage-close-decision.json

