Leak x1.5 meets the gain bands?</attribute><attribute class="java.lang.String" key="note">E04 | Leak x1.5 meets the gain bands?

Status: NO

Method: Structural dissection / reversible intervention

Scope / coordinates: g2-leak-150 versus B3; all registered regions; SP3 stage G.

Remaining search space: That tested intervention meets every registered gain/preservation band or fails at least one.

Binary predicate: g2-leak-150 satisfies every stage-G gain and preservation clause.

Decision limit: Registered stage-G bands, including 310 pA count &gt;=8 and preservation of sweep-43 return.

Recorded observation: Counts become 0/0/6 at 200/250/310 pA; late return shifts about -3.8 mV. Registered clauses fail.

YES: Retain the correction for independent validation.

NO: Exclude this leak dose as a sufficient correction with the preserved controls.

Next check: Carry forward the failed tested dose; distinguish the unrun combined arm in E05.

Unresolved after either answer: No continuous-dose theorem or exhaustive passive-family exclusion is established by this single dose.

